(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// sys.settrace (queue 219t; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 219t\"): the legacy tracer as sys.monitoring's tool 7"] [4 1 "// (PY_MONITORING_SYS_TRACE_ID), beside 220's profiler (tool 6, monitoring.go), as CPython 3.14.10's"] [5 1 "// Python/legacy_tracing.c makes it (PSF License Agreement): PY_START, PY_RESUME and PY_THROW are 'call', PY_RETURN and"] [6 1 "// PY_YIELD 'return' with the value, PY_UNWIND 'return' with None, RAISE 'exception' with (type, value, traceback); the"] [7 1 "// local events LINE (and the legacy JUMP and INSTRUCTION: a backward jump's 'line', 'opcode') from the dispatch loop"] [8 1 "// (traceInstr), by Python/instrumentation.c's rule over pyi's IR (initialize_lines, _Py_call_instrumentation_line). The"] [9 1 "// trampoline is Python/sysmodule.c's trace_trampoline. f_lineno's jumps are Objects/frameobject.c's"] [10 1 "// frame_lineno_set_impl over mark_stacks, ported to pyi's IR."] [11 1 "//"] [12 1 "// While a trace function is set (or a tool has LINE, INSTRUCTION or JUMP events: monTraceMask), frames run on the loop:"] [13 1 "// guardedStep and step enter a code object's compiled body only when tracing is off, and a compiled frame already"] [14 1 "// running returns AotToLoop at its next block start (arbace.python.aot's check, AotTracing), its whole stack in the"] [15 1 "// frame, guardedStep continuing it on the loop."] [17 1 "// the events' numbers beyond monitoring.go's"] [28 2 "// monTraceTool is the legacy tracer's tool (PY_MONITORING_SYS_TRACE_ID)"] [30 2 "// monTraceMask are the events the loop reports: while one is set no frame runs compiled"] [32 2 "// traceEvents are the legacy tracer's (legacy_tracing.c's _PyEval_SetTrace)"] [38 2 "// traceFuncs are the threads' trace functions (tstate->c_traceobj)"] [40 2 "// traceWhat is the event of the trace function a thread runs (tstate->what_event), absent when none: f_lineno's"] [41 2 "// setter reads it"] [45 1 "// AotToLoop is a compiled body's answer at a block start while tracing (queue 219t): f.PC is the block start, the whole"] [46 1 "// value stack in f.Stack; guardedStep runs the frame on the loop from there."] [53 1 "// AotTracing is whether frames must run on the loop (a trace function or a line tool set): the compiled code's check"] [54 1 "// at each block start and after each direct call."] [67 1 "// setTrace is _PyEval_SetTrace for t: fn None removes it."] [77 1 "// traceCall is trace_trampoline: the 'call' event to the thread's trace function, the others to f's f_trace; a result"] [78 1 "// other than None becomes f_trace; an error removes the trace function and f_trace and is returned."] [117 1 "// traceEvent is the legacy tracer's callback for the frame events (monFire's native)."] [141 1 "// monRaise is RAISE at f (runFrames, where the frame's traceback entry is added: CPython's monitor_raise at its error"] [142 1 "// label, not at a re-raise); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [153 1 "// genWrapped is whether c's view ends with the handler codegen wraps a generator's or coroutine's body in"] [154 1 "// (CALL_INTRINSIC_1 INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR, RERAISE 1; queue 281): an exception leaving the frame is handled there"] [155 1 "// and raised again (EXCEPTION_HANDLED, RERAISE)."] [165 1 "// monExc is an exception event ev (RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED) at f; a callback's error replaces the exception."] [176 1 "// monStopIteration is STOP_ITERATION at f (monitor_stop_iteration): a generator or coroutine a yield-from ran to its end"] [177 1 "// with value v, a StopIteration(v) made for the event; RAISE (gen false) for the StopIteration a non-generator delegate"] [178 1 "// raised or a generator's next set for a value other than None (gen_iternext)."] [187 2 "// PyErr_SetObject(PyExc_StopIteration, value): no argument for None"] [195 1 "// traceLines are c's instructions that may start a line event (initialize_lines): a line different from the previous"] [196 1 "// instruction's in code order, a jump's target but a for-iter's, a handler's target; never the RESUME nop at 0."] [214 2 "// FOR_ITER's target is not marked: CPython's is the POP_ITER after its END_FOR, which never starts a line (queue 248)"] [232 1 "// resumeAt0 is whether c starts with its RESUME, the nop arbace.python.compile puts at co_firstlineno (a module has none)."] [237 1 "// traceInstr is the loop's hook before f runs instruction f.PC while tracing: the line event (a line's instrumented"] [238 1 "// instruction reached from another line, or after a RESUME: the frame's start, a resumption after a yield), the opcode"] [239 1 "// event, a backward jump's line event. A trace function's jump (f_lineno) changes f.PC: the target then runs with no"] [240 1 "// event of its own. An error is raised at the instruction."] [258 3 "// JUMP, BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT of the instruction that led here (queue 281)"] [288 3 "// INSTRUCTION: the view's instructions this one came from (a branch's NOT_TAKEN and a loop's POP_ITER are"] [289 3 "// monFlow's, as the path decides them; the view's RESUME fires none)"] [293 5 "// the view's instructions of no IR instruction just before this one's (PUSH_NULL ...), reached in sequence"] [294 5 "// from prev's"] [340 1 "// monFlowFrame and monFlowPC are the frame a JUMP or BRANCH callback runs for and the destination its stack is"] [341 1 "// (f_lineno's setter; under the GIL, no event fires inside a callback)."] [347 1 "// monFlowFire fires a JUMP or BRANCH event (args: the code, its source and destination offsets) of prev to pc: f_lasti"] [348 1 "// the jump while the callbacks run (INSTRUMENTED_JUMP's frame), a callback's f_lineno jump kept (f.PC moved)."] [361 1 "// monFlow is the JUMP or BRANCH event of IR instruction prev, a jump, that led to pc (queue 281): CPython's"] [362 1 "// INSTRUMENTED_JUMP_FORWARD/BACKWARD (JUMP), INSTRUMENTED_POP_JUMP_IF_* (BRANCH_RIGHT, taken), INSTRUMENTED_NOT_TAKEN"] [363 1 "// (BRANCH_LEFT, from the jump past the NOT_TAKEN), INSTRUMENTED_FOR_ITER (BRANCH_LEFT, a next value) and"] [364 1 "// INSTRUMENTED_POP_ITER (BRANCH_RIGHT, the loop's end, past the POP_ITER), their offsets the view's (bytecode_asm.go) for"] [365 1 "// the view's instruction the IR's came from. An IR jump the view has no jump for fires nothing."] [372 3 "// an async for's step: the awaited __anext__'s END_SEND then NOT_TAKEN (BRANCH_LEFT from the END_SEND), its"] [373 3 "// StopAsyncIteration's END_ASYNC_FOR (BRANCH_RIGHT from the END_SEND past it)"] [469 4 "// past the END_FOR the exhausted FOR_ITER skips, the POP_ITER fires the event"] [492 1 "// f_lineno's jumps: the kinds of mark_stacks' slots, three bits each in an int64 (the top the low bits)"] [538 1 "// irEffect is instruction in's stack effect falling through and jumping (arbace.python.ir's table)."] [595 1 "// markStacks is mark_stacks over c's IR: each instruction's stack as its slots' kinds, stackUninit where unreached."] [714 1 "// frameSetLineno is frame_lineno_set_impl: a jump to line v from a trace function's event."] [743 2 "// marklines: each line's first instruction in code order"] [766 29 "// a JUMP or BRANCH callback's: f_lasti the jump, the stack its destination's"] [816 24 "// the value the yield popped"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[96 20] [124 35] [144 76] [145 29] [167 71] [168 29] [218 21] [224 24] [259 35] [270 51] [275 91] [283 58] [290 23] [301 20] [301 31] [305 51] [313 26] [316 43] [321 63] [328 50] [387 55] [456 24] [471 23] [471 39] [475 21] [479 28] [569 13] [569 21] [608 18] [608 24] [610 13] [610 20] [645 9] [645 16] [648 9] [648 16] [716 22] [746 12] [746 19] [748 20] [770 12] [770 19] [806 103]]} (go/file "trace.go" :imports [])

;; sys.settrace (queue 219t; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "Design: 219t"): the legacy tracer as sys.monitoring's tool 7
;; (PY_MONITORING_SYS_TRACE_ID), beside 220's profiler (tool 6, monitoring.go), as CPython 3.14.10's
;; Python/legacy_tracing.c makes it (PSF License Agreement): PY_START, PY_RESUME and PY_THROW are 'call', PY_RETURN and
;; PY_YIELD 'return' with the value, PY_UNWIND 'return' with None, RAISE 'exception' with (type, value, traceback); the
;; local events LINE (and the legacy JUMP and INSTRUCTION: a backward jump's 'line', 'opcode') from the dispatch loop
;; (traceInstr), by Python/instrumentation.c's rule over pyi's IR (initialize_lines, _Py_call_instrumentation_line). The
;; trampoline is Python/sysmodule.c's trace_trampoline. f_lineno's jumps are Objects/frameobject.c's
;; frame_lineno_set_impl over mark_stacks, ported to pyi's IR.
;;
;; While a trace function is set (or a tool has LINE, INSTRUCTION or JUMP events: monTraceMask), frames run on the loop:
;; guardedStep and step enter a code object's compiled body only when tracing is off, and a compiled frame already
;; running returns AotToLoop at its next block start (arbace.python.aot's check, AotTracing), its whole stack in the
;; frame, guardedStep continuing it on the loop.


